{"content":[{"c":["HANDMAID, HANDMAIDEN*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Female servants. They were familiar members among many households in biblical days. The handmaid cared for the women and children of a family and served as the woman’s personal attendant. She enjoyed the protection of the law (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.25.6","r":"Lev.25.6","rawR":"Lev.25.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.25.6","value":"Lev.25.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 25:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.5.14","r":"Deut.5.14","rawR":"Deut.5.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.5.14","value":"Deut.5.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 5:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.15.12-15","r":"Deut.15.12-15","rawR":"Deut.15.12-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.15.12-15","value":"Deut.15.12-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:12-15"},"), and as a free wife’s maid, sometimes became a concubine where there was a childless marriage (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.30.3","r":"Gen.30.3","rawR":"Gen.30.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.30.3","value":"Gen.30.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 30:3"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HandmaidHandmaiden","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Lv 25:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.25.6","rawQueryValue":"Lev.25.6","sourceRefExact":"Lev.25.6"},{"anchorText":"Dt 5:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.5.14","rawQueryValue":"Deut.5.14","sourceRefExact":"Deut.5.14"},{"anchorText":"15:12-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.15.12-15","rawQueryValue":"Deut.15.12-15","sourceRefExact":"Deut.15.12-15"},{"anchorText":"Gn 30:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.30.3","rawQueryValue":"Gen.30.3","sourceRefExact":"Gen.30.3"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"74577affe9240b49523c08fce3816da127c